WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.014 --> 00:00:02.010
- Ugh, yikes.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.630
I just wanna say that I
would never ever make this

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.384
for myself, but I really hope he likes it.

00:00:08.384 --> 00:00:10.390
(light music)

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.398
- Hello!

00:00:11.398 --> 00:00:12.980
- [Woman] Hi Jackson.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.092
How are you doing?

00:00:14.092 --> 00:00:14.925
- [Jackson] Good!

00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:15.758
- Good.

00:00:15.758 --> 00:00:16.591
Okay, cool.

00:00:16.591 --> 00:00:19.070
So, if you could have any
dish in the world today,

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.420
what would you have?

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.420
- It will be dragon fire chicken
with pizza stuffed inside.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.100
- What is that supposed to mean?

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.560
What is dragon fire supposed to mean?

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.100
Maybe you could draw it for
me and help me out a little.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.680
- [Jackson] Here's a chicken part.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.600
- Okay, is it just a
regular chicken flavor?

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.553
Does it have, is it garlicky?

00:00:41.553 --> 00:00:43.220
Is it spicy?

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.310
- Spicy.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.930
- Spicy, you like spicy food?

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:47.940
Whoa, okay.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.360
What's spicy to a kid?

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.069
Like, how much spice can he handle?

00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:53.220
You know, I don't want
to go too overboard,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:57.030
so, I'm just gonna you know,
tiptoe into spicy territory.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.168
Oh that's a big chicken.

00:00:58.168 --> 00:01:00.550
Let's talk about the pizza.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.780
- [Jackson] Here's a pizza.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.040
- [Alexis] What toppings do you like?

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.280
- [Jackson] Peppers.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.170
- Peppers?

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.320
Does it have pepperoni?

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.706
- Yes.
- Yes? Okay.

00:01:08.706 --> 00:01:11.078
Okay, green and red peppers,

00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:14.048
pepperoni pizza.

00:01:14.048 --> 00:01:15.502
- [Jackson] Here's the dragon.

00:01:15.502 --> 00:01:17.043
- That's the dragon?

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:21.403
You know there's a full on
dragon inside of this chicken.

00:01:21.403 --> 00:01:22.236
What?

00:01:22.236 --> 00:01:25.290
I mean, I don't know what I'm gonna do.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.610
And you said that there's dragon flames?

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:28.780
- [Jackson] Uh huh.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.670
- What do dragon flames taste like?

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.260
- It tastes like olives.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.470
- I would assume dragon
fire could be like ketchup.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.580
Or you know, something like red and saucy.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.523
And he said tastes like olive.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.020
Okay, this is really helpful.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.150
Thank you so much.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.939
I mean, I'm gonna try my best.

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:46.390
Do you believe in me?

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.862
- Yes.
- Yes? Okay.

00:01:47.862 --> 00:01:49.712
That's the vote of confidence I need.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:52.860
My plan, we'll see how it goes,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.650
I'm going to pound a
chicken breast really thin,

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.770
put a bunch of spices
on it, not too spicy.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.470
And then fill it with
marinara, mozzarella,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.480
peppers, pepperoni,

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.030
roll it up, and then I'm
gonna take puff pastry

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:07.410
and brush it with tapenade.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.580
And then I'm gonna put the chicken inside

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.250
of the puff pastry and wrap it up.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.520
That way you have some of
the like, dough component

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.090
of what pizza could be.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.460
And it's gonna hold it all together,

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.600
so it's not gonna be like this giant mess.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.880
I don't know if that's really gonna work.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.370
But, we'll see.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.370
Okay, so I'm gonna start with
just a tiny bit of cayenne.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.970
Cayenne's pretty aggressive
and Jackson is six.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:31.610
So don't want to get too crazy.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.500
Some Italian seasoning,
paprika, maybe that's like a nod

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.820
to fire and flames too.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:38.920
Two teaspoons of salt.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.170
A little pepper, so he
wanted red and green peppers.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.700
There's not gonna be that
much room for filling,

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.330
so I don't think we need that much.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.080
I was thinking that the
pepperoni should be layered,

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.013
but maybe it should be chopped.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.073
Anyone?

00:02:53.073 --> 00:02:53.906
- [Voiceover] Full pepperoni.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:54.739
- Full pepperoni, okay.

00:02:54.739 --> 00:02:57.840
So now we're gonna pound
the chicken breast.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.108
Gonna wash my hands.

00:02:59.108 --> 00:03:01.608
(light music)

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.522
And just gonna go for it.

00:03:05.522 --> 00:03:08.230
(mallet pounds)

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.850
So I feel like pounding the
chicken breast really thin

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.045
is just gonna give more
options for filling it.

00:03:14.045 --> 00:03:16.288
It might not be what he intended,

00:03:16.288 --> 00:03:18.654
you know, artistic,

00:03:18.654 --> 00:03:22.302
(classical music)

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:23.493
what the (bleeps) the word?

00:03:23.493 --> 00:03:24.326
- [Voiceover] Creative liberty.

00:03:24.326 --> 00:03:25.159
- Thank you.

00:03:25.159 --> 00:03:26.451
I was gonna say liability,
and it was like,

00:03:26.451 --> 00:03:27.440
[Voiceover] Liability?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.633
Yeah, but taking a creative,

00:03:30.897 --> 00:03:31.930
- [Voiceover] Liberty.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.040
- Liberty.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.690
So, spiced chicken (laughs)

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.190
I'm gonna wash my hands again.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.340
Sorry, I forgot that the
oven needs to be pre-heated

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.173
so I just did that.

00:03:43.173 --> 00:03:45.233
Let me just check the
temperature, one sec.

00:03:45.233 --> 00:03:46.070
- [Voiceover] Sorry, what?

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:47.800
- Oh no, I'm just talking to myself.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.590
Now I'm gonna layer some mozzarella

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:53.000
on top of this ruby chicken.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.460
I think a layer of pepperoni.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.560
He seemed really enthusiastic
about the peppers.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.900
Like, this feels like a
lot to me, but we'll see.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.540
Oh, and another layer of cheese,

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.960
kids love cheese, it's tasty.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.360
Okay.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.810
So, okay so this giant chicken mound,

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.430
okay this cheese clearly needs to leave.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.830
So we have this like weird chicken log

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:16.703
that we're gonna chill in the
refrigerator for a little bit.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:19.910
My work here is done.

00:04:22.503 --> 00:04:24.460
I forgot marinara sauce.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.360
Oh no, it's like kind of crucial to pizza.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.390
Should I unwrap it?

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.463
What should I do?

00:04:29.463 --> 00:04:30.296
- [Voiceover] Yeah.

00:04:30.296 --> 00:04:31.832
- (bleeps) Okay.

00:04:31.832 --> 00:04:33.070
Agh, okay.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:34.370
Back again.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.530
Okay, oh boy.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.326
This is like, what am I doing?

00:04:38.326 --> 00:04:40.710
Okay, back to the fridge.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.550
So, now that the chicken
is chilling for a bit,

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.030
I'm gonna roll out the puff pastry and see

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.452
if I can make some puff pastry flames.

00:04:47.452 --> 00:04:48.760
(laughs)

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.440
Does this look like a flame?

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.660
I don't know, it looks
like a sad turkey hand.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:57.460
Like, maybe it needs some
more, like, flames on flames.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.835
Like layers of flames.

00:04:58.835 --> 00:05:00.073
What? Huh?

00:05:00.073 --> 00:05:02.210
You know, actually if you
hold this upside down,

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.050
it could almost look like this flame.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.100
I feel like the bone is more
successful than the fire.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.786
It unfortunately does
look like a dog bone.

00:05:09.786 --> 00:05:12.130
I feel like he could have, you know,

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.400
he could have tried to
do something similar.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:19.030
Now I'm going to brush the puff
pastry with olive tapenade.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:22.000
Since dragon flames taste
like olive, of course.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.270
With beef wellington you
have a layer of like,

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.020
minced mushrooms called duxelles.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.550
So, maybe the tapenade won't be that bad.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:32.853
So, just gonna fold it
up like a little present.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:36.840
Okay, so it turns out that this is smaller

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:37.760
than I anticipated.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.870
So maybe there's only room for one flame.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.940
I think the flames can overlap.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.640
It looks like a dragon egg.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.040
Hey, that's a really good start.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.480
So I'm gonna brush it in egg wash,

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.290
sprinkle it with flaky sea salt,

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.010
because you know, I
doubt Jackson will care,

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.750
but I just feel like it'll
make it a little nicer.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.715
And in the oven it goes.

00:05:57.715 --> 00:06:00.650
The bones a little dark.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.720
So this needs some more time,
but I need to remove this

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:07.190
so I don't feed him a
totally charred bone.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:09.430
This is not my best planning, let's say.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.960
It actually looks better
than I anticipated.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:13.390
I feel like the flames actually

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.690
really came to life in baking.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.410
It did explode a bit on the bottom,

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.830
but he's not gonna see that.

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.400
And I know, it didn't call for parsley.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.935
But I just can't help myself.

00:06:21.935 --> 00:06:24.852
(loud choir sings)

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.680
Jackson's about to eat
this weird creation.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.750
I don't know if he was expecting
this kind of interpretation

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.450
but I feel like it looks good.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.715
And I hope the flavors work together.

00:06:37.715 --> 00:06:39.341
Crossin' my fingers.

00:06:39.341 --> 00:06:42.048
Are you ready to see what I made?

00:06:42.048 --> 00:06:42.881
- Yes.

00:06:42.881 --> 00:06:43.827
- Okay.

00:06:43.827 --> 00:06:45.910
(laughs)

00:06:47.796 --> 00:06:50.660
Okay, so everything is inside.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.540
So the chicken, and pizza
stuff is all inside of here.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.790
What do you think so far?

00:06:55.928 --> 00:06:57.860
(laughs) Okay, lets' see.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:58.693
Do you want to try it?

00:06:58.693 --> 00:06:59.664
- Yes.
- Yes!

00:06:59.664 --> 00:07:00.910
- [Jackson] That's a huge knife.

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.910
- It is a huge knife.

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:03.930
Whoa.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:07.270
So there's the chicken, and
inside there's pepperoni

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:10.750
and cheese, and peppers,
there's olives on the outside

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.750
of it because that's what you
said dragon flames taste like.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:15.924
Okay, ready?

00:07:15.924 --> 00:07:19.540
(fast saxophone music)

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.770
Is it spicy?

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:21.910
Too spicy?

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:22.933
Oh no!

00:07:23.889 --> 00:07:24.750
(gags)

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.583
Oh no.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:28.233
Too spicy.

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:33.570
Okay, so I'm a little
afraid to do this now,

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:36.930
but if you had to rate
this dish in emojis,

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.853
here are all your choices.

00:07:38.853 --> 00:07:39.710
(laughs)

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.899
That's probably accurate!

00:07:41.899 --> 00:07:43.930
(laughs)

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.133
You know what, that's a fair assessment.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.710
It's not that bad.

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:51.833
- [Jackson] Which one?

00:07:51.833 --> 00:07:54.335
(laughs)

00:07:54.335 --> 00:07:55.630
I think I'm this one.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:56.463
It's not that bad.

00:07:56.463 --> 00:07:58.440
It kinda tastes like pizza chicken.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:00.674
Maybe if it wasn't spicy
it would have been better.

00:08:00.674 --> 00:08:02.460
(playful instrumental music)

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.190
Take some creative liberties to make sure

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:07.245
this isn't absolutely repulsive, so.

00:08:07.245 --> 00:08:09.492
(laughs)

00:08:09.492 --> 00:08:11.161
(friendly chatter)

00:08:11.161 --> 00:08:15.187
(playful instrumental music)

00:08:15.187 --> 00:08:16.880
(snaps)

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:20.630
(playful instrumental music)

